<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to January 22 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.36 (0.36)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.45 (0.45)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  0.91 (0.93)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.32 (0.32)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.40 (0.40)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.30)	 three years  0.86 (0.88)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.28 (0.28)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.35 (0.35)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.25 (0.25)	 three years  0.81 (0.83)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Jan 20-Jan 24:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.51 (0.50)   120-150 days  0.55 (0.54)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.52 (0.51)   150-180 days  UNQ  (0.55)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.52 (0.52)   180-360 days  0.55 (0.54)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.53 (0.53)   over 360 days 0.46 (0.40)</p>
